jsp-375 pack: content licence
=============================

1. Attribution statement

Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government
Licence v3.0.

2. Source identification

Source: JSP 375: Management of Health and Safety in Defence, Directive &
Guidance Version 1.7 (06 February 2025), together with Volume 1 arrangements
chapters and Volume 3 high-risk activities on the defence estate chapters
from the GOV.UK JSP 375 collection attachment set used for this build,
Ministry of Defence (Director Defence Safety), © Crown copyright.

3. Source links

Collection page:
https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/jsp-375-health-and-safety-handbook
Directive publication page (Volume 1 handbook entry hosting Directive PDF):
https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/jsp-375-health-and-safety-handbook-volume-1
Arrangements (Volume 1 chapters) publication page:
https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/jsp-375-health-and-safety-handbook-volume-2
Volume 3 publication page:
https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/jsp-375-health-and-safety-handbook-volume-3

Publication pages carry the gov.uk footer sentence: "All content is
available under the Open Government Licence v3.0, except where otherwise
stated" (pages fetched 2026-11-22).

4. Licence

Open Government Licence v3.0:
https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/

5. Nature of this pack

This pack contains reconstructed reference notes, not reproductions.
Content was restructured and summarised from the source; passages are
paraphrased except short defined terms.

6. Non-endorsement

Nothing in this pack suggests that the Ministry of Defence endorses it or
that it has any official status.

7. Excluded material

- MOD crests and logos, and military insignia.
- Verbatim safety rule-book procedure dumps from Volume 3 person-in-charge books.
- MOD form field templates (forms cited by title/role only).

8. Scope

This licence governs the content of this pack (SKILL.md, chapters/,
glossary.md, cheatsheet.md, patterns.md). The repository's MIT licence
covers tooling and scaffolding only.

9. Per-source record (summary)

